1
00:00:02,254 --> 00:00:10,050
在 MLOps 出现之前，从数据科学家的笔记本到上线应用的路径是一个破碎且令人沮丧的过程。
Before mOps, the path from a data scientist's laptop to a live application was a broken, frustrating process.

2
00:00:10,542 --> 00:00:12,650
我们称之为「巨大的鸿沟」。
We call this the Great Divide.

3
00:00:13,190 --> 00:00:18,090
在一侧，数据科学家在隔离的笔记本里创建出色的模型。
On one side, data scientists created brilliant models in isolated notebooks.

4
00:00:18,670 --> 00:00:22,830
在另一侧，运维团队则在苦苦支撑着应用程序的运行。
On the other, an operations team struggled to keep applications running.

5
00:00:23,502 --> 00:00:33,410
它们之间的衔接是手动且容易出错的，导致了那句臭名昭
著的话：但在我的机器上是正常的，这造成了延误和失败。
The journey between them was a manual, error-prone handover that led to the
infamous phrase, but it worked on my machine, causing delays and failures.

6
00:00:34,126 --> 00:00:36,900
那么，MLOps 到底是什么？
So, what exactly is MLOps?

7
00:00:37,582 --> 00:00:47,230
它是一种文化和一套实践，旨在将机器学习系统（ML）的开发与其运维和部署（Ops）统一起来。
It's a culture and a set of practices that aims to unify the development
of machine learning systems, ML, with their operation and deployment, Ops.

8
00:00:47,918 --> 00:00:50,550
它不仅仅是一个工具，更是一种理念。
It's not just a tool, but a philosophy.

9
00:00:51,182 --> 00:00:54,070
为了更好地理解它，让我们拆解一下这个名字。
To understand it better, let's break down its name.

10
00:00:54,638 --> 00:01:00,710
它是三个关键领域的融合——机器学习、开发和运维。
It's a fusion of three critical disciplines – machine learning, development, and operations.

11
00:01:01,390 --> 00:01:09,150
为了直观理解 MLOps 的解决方案，你可以把它想象成
在为你的机器学习模型建立一个复杂的自动化工厂。
To visualize the MLOps solution, think of it as building a sophisticated, automated factory for your machine learning models.

12
00:01:09,790 --> 00:01:15,810
MLOps 不是在各个孤岛之间手动搬运零件，而是构建了一条高科技的流水线。
Instead of manually carrying parts between islands, MLOps constructs a high-tech assembly line.

13
00:01:16,190 --> 00:01:28,330
这条流水线实现了从处理原始数据到构建、测试、部署和
监控模型的全自动化，确保了快速、可靠且可重复的流程。
This assembly line automates everything from processing raw data to building, testing, deploying, and monitoring models,
ensuring a fast, reliable, and repeatable process.

14
00:01:28,710 --> 00:01:33,870
这个 AI 工厂是我们贯穿整个大师课程的核心概念。
This AI factory is the core concept we'll build throughout this masterclass.

15
00:01:34,450 --> 00:01:41,290
既然我们了解了是什么和为什么，现在来看看我们 AI 工厂的蓝图——MLOps 生命周期。
Now that we understand the what and why, let's look at the blueprint for our AI factory, the MLOps lifecycle.

16
00:01:42,094 --> 00:01:45,750
这是一个持续迭代的过程，而不是线性的过程。
This is a continuous, iterative process, not a linear one.

17
00:01:46,254 --> 00:01:51,090
它引导模型从一个简单的想法变成一个不断改进的生产资产。
It guides a model from a simple idea to a constantly improving production asset.

18
00:01:51,090 --> 00:02:02,370
我们将这个生命周期作为我们的路线图，在接下来的片段中，我们将深入探讨每个阶段，
首先从机器学习的基石——数据本身开始。
We'll use this lifecycle as our roadmap, and in the upcoming scenes, we'll dive deep into each stage,
starting with the foundation of all machine learning – the data itself.

19
00:02:02,862 --> 00:02:06,710
我们的旅程从第一阶段开始——数据工程。
Our journey begins with the first stage – data engineering.

20
00:02:07,438 --> 00:02:10,669
这就是我们获取、准备和管理数据的地方。
This is where we source, prepare, and manage our data.

21
00:02:11,374 --> 00:02:21,630
它涉及从各种来源摄入原始数据，验证其质量以尽早发现错误，并将其转换为整洁、可用的格式。
It involves ingesting raw data from various sources, validating its quality
to catch errors early and transforming it into a clean, usable format.

22
00:02:22,350 --> 00:02:26,130
你可以把它想象成为我们的工厂采购高质量的原材料。
Think of this as sourcing high-quality raw materials for our factory.

23
00:02:26,702 --> 00:02:29,970
如果没有好的数据，即使是最好的模型也会失败。
Without good data, even the best model will fail.

24
00:02:30,550 --> 00:02:35,250
在数据工程中，一个关键的 MLOps 实践是数据版本控制。
Within data engineering, a critical MLOps practice is data versioning.

25
00:02:35,694 --> 00:02:40,190
就像我们对代码进行版本控制一样，我们也必须对数据集进行版本控制。
Just like we version control our code, we must version control our datasets.

26
00:02:41,006 --> 00:02:46,150
这意味着记录下用于训练特定模型版本的精确数据快照。
This means taking a snapshot of the exact data used to train a specific model version.

27
00:02:46,150 --> 00:02:49,850
这一实践是可重复性的基石。
This practice is the bedrock of reproducibility.

28
00:02:50,574 --> 00:02:58,530
如果模型表现异常，我们可以追溯到它训练时使用的精确数据，这对于调试和审计至关重要。
If a model behaves unexpectedly, we can trace it back to the exact
data it was trained on, which is crucial for debugging and auditing.

29
00:02:59,090 --> 00:03:04,870
随着 MLOps 的成熟，一个专门的工具变得必不可少，那就是特征仓库（Feature Store）。
As MLOps has matured, a specialized tool has become essential, the Feature Store.

30
00:03:05,486 --> 00:03:13,810
这是一个中心化的仓库，用于管理和提供经过筛选的数据特征，供模型训练和实时推理使用。
This is a centralized repository that manages and serves curated data features for both model training and real-time inference.

31
00:03:14,318 --> 00:03:21,250
与其让每个数据科学家各自独立创建特征，不如将它们标准化并存储在这里。
Instead of each data scientist creating their own features in isolation, they are standardized and stored here.

32
00:03:21,838 --> 00:03:26,030
这为整个组织提供了特征的单一事实来源。
This provides a single source of truth for features across the organization.

33
00:03:26,770 --> 00:03:31,490
特征仓库解决的最关键问题是训练与推理的偏差。
The most critical problem a feature store solves is training-serving skew.

34
00:03:32,046 --> 00:03:39,990
这种模型的「隐形杀手」发生在训练时使用的特征与实时预测时使用的特征计算方式不同时。
This silent killer of models occurs when the features used for training
are calculated differently than the features used for live predictions.

35
00:03:39,990 --> 00:03:48,070
例如，在训练中通过批处理计算的特征，可能与在推理中实时计算的特征不同。
For example, a feature calculated in a batch process for training might differ from one calculated in real-time for serving.

36
00:03:48,686 --> 00:03:56,430
特征仓库确保两种情况下使用的特征逻辑完全一致，从而消除这个常见的故障源。
The feature store ensures the exact same feature logic is used in both cases, eliminating this common source of failure.

37
00:03:57,030 --> 00:04:01,790
在数据准备并完成版本控制后，我们进入第二阶段：模型开发。
With our data prepared and versioned, we move to the second stage, model development.

38
00:04:02,510 --> 00:04:09,070
这是创意阶段，数据科学家在此探索数据、工程化特征并训练各种模型。
This is the creative phase where data scientists explore data, engineer features, and train various models.

39
00:04:09,070 --> 00:04:13,450
在 MLOps 环境下，这并不是一个随意进行的流程。
In an MLOps context, this is not a free-form process.

40
00:04:14,050 --> 00:04:16,950
核心实践之一是严格的实验跟踪。
A core practice is rigorous experiment tracking.

41
00:04:17,670 --> 00:04:24,610
每一个实验，包括代码版本、数据版本、参数以及生成的指标，都会被自动记录。
Every experiment, including the code version, data version, parameters, and resulting metrics, is logged automatically.

42
00:04:25,358 --> 00:04:29,850
这创建了一个可审计且可复现的所有建模尝试的历史记录。
This creates an auditable and reproducible history of all modeling attempts.

43
00:04:30,550 --> 00:04:36,750
一旦通过实验确定了一个有前景的模型，我们就需要为自动化流水线做好准备。
Once a promising model is identified through experimentation, we need to prepare it for the automated pipeline.

44
00:04:36,750 --> 00:04:45,470
这包括将模型及其所有依赖项（如特定的库版本）打包成标准化的、可移植的格式。
This involves packaging the model and all its dependencies, like specific library versions, into a standardized, portable format.

45
00:04:46,094 --> 00:04:50,010
最常用的方法是容器化，使用像 Docker 这样的工具。
The most common method is containerization, using tools like Docker.

46
00:04:50,670 --> 00:05:02,810
这创建了一个自包含的容器，可以在任何环境中一致运行，从开发者的笔记本电脑到生产服务器，
彻底解决「在我机器上能跑」的问题。
This creates a self-contained box that can run consistently in any environment, from a developer's laptop to a production server,
solving the it-worked-on-my-machine problem once and for all.

47
00:05:03,374 --> 00:05:10,350
现在，我们来到了 AI 工厂的发动机室：自动化的 CI-CD-CT 流水线。
Now, we arrive at the engine room of our AI factory, the automated CI-CD-CT pipeline.

48
00:05:11,214 --> 00:05:14,190
这就是我们将讨论过的所有组件连接在一起的地方。
This is where we connect all the pieces we've discussed.

49
00:05:14,958 --> 00:05:20,070
这个流水线实现了我们打包好的模型的构建、测试和部署自动化。
This pipeline automates the building, testing, and deployment of our packaged model.

50
00:05:20,750 --> 00:05:25,830
例如，当数据科学家提交新代码时，它就会被自动触发。
It is triggered automatically, for instance, when a data scientist commits new code.

51
00:05:26,542 --> 00:05:29,450
让我们分解一下这个流水线的三个组成部分。
Let's break down the three components of this pipeline.

52
00:05:30,126 --> 00:05:35,030
持续集成、持续交付和持续训练。
continuous integration, continuous delivery, and continuous training.

53
00:05:35,694 --> 00:05:39,670
我们流水线的第一个步骤是持续集成，也就是 CI。
The first step in our pipeline is continuous integration, or CI.

54
00:05:40,494 --> 00:05:44,130
在软件工程中，CI 侧重于代码测试。
In software engineering, CI focuses on testing code.

55
00:05:44,718 --> 00:05:47,110
而在 MLOps 中，CI 的范围要广得多。
In MLOps, CI is much broader.

56
00:05:47,710 --> 00:05:57,710
它不仅包括代码单元测试，还包括数据验证、基于基准的模型验证，甚至还有公平性和偏差检查。
It includes not just code unit tests, but also automated tests for data validation,
model validation against a baseline, and even checks for fairness and bias.

57
00:05:58,254 --> 00:06:03,396
只有通过这一整套综合测试，模型才能进入下一个阶段。
A model only proceeds to the next stage if it passes this comprehensive suite of tests.

58
00:06:04,174 --> 00:06:10,170
模型通过所有 CI 检查后，就由持续交付，也就是 CD，接手。
After a model passes all CI checks, continuous delivery, or CD, takes over.

59
00:06:10,830 --> 00:06:13,110
这个阶段实现了发布流程的自动化。
This stage automates the release process.

60
00:06:13,710 --> 00:06:22,210
打包好的模型首先被推送到模型注册表，这是一个所有生产就绪模型产物的中央版本控制仓库。
The packaged model is first pushed to a model registry, which is a central
version-controlled repository for all production-ready model artifacts.

61
00:06:22,210 --> 00:06:32,010
从注册表开始，CD 系统可以自动将模型部署到预发布环境进行最终测试，并最终部署到生产环境。
From the registry, the CD system can then automatically deploy the model
to a staging environment for final testing and, ultimately, to production.

62
00:06:32,590 --> 00:06:39,530
在持续交付中，成熟的 MLOps 实践会使用复杂的部署策略来降低风险。
Within continuous delivery, mature MLOps practices use sophisticated deployment strategies to minimize risk.

63
00:06:40,450 --> 00:06:49,550
与其采用大爆炸式发布，我们可以使用金丝雀发布等策略，
最初仅让一小部分用户流量接触新模型。
Instead of a big bang release, we can use strategies like a canary release,
where the new model is initially exposed to a small fraction of user traffic.

64
00:06:50,030 --> 00:06:55,790
我们密切监控其表现，如果表现良好，再逐步推给所有人。
We monitor its performance closely, and if it performs well, we gradually roll it out to everyone.

65
00:06:56,462 --> 00:06:59,990
这让我们能在对用户影响最小的情况下发现问题。
This allows us to catch problems with minimal impact on users.

66
00:07:00,590 --> 00:07:07,490
我们流水线的最后一部分是持续训练，也就是 CT，这是 MLOps 中非常独特的一个概念。
The final piece of our pipeline is Continuous Training, or CT, a concept largely unique to MLOps.

67
00:07:08,046 --> 00:07:13,090
CT 是在生产环境中自动重新训练和重新部署模型的过程。
CT is the automated process of retraining and redeploying models in production.

68
00:07:13,590 --> 00:07:17,730
这并不是指数据科学家手动启动新的训练任务。
This isn't about a data scientist manually kicking off a new training job.

69
00:07:17,934 --> 00:07:29,790
相反，系统被设计为根据计划、新数据的可用性，或者正如我们接下来将看到的，
根据在线模型性能下降来自动触发重新训练。
Instead, the system is designed to automatically trigger retraining based on a schedule, the availability of significant new data, or,
as we'll see next, a decline in the live model's performance.

70
00:07:30,446 --> 00:07:33,230
模型部署后，旅程并没有结束。
With our model deployed, the journey isn't over.

71
00:07:33,550 --> 00:07:35,030
事实上，它才刚刚开始。
In fact, it's just beginning.

72
00:07:35,758 --> 00:07:39,130
我们现在进入至关重要的持续监控阶段。
We now enter the crucial, ongoing stage of monitoring.

73
00:07:39,910 --> 00:07:45,070
关键在于，我们必须监控的不仅仅是 CPU 使用率或延迟等系统健康状况。
Crucially, we must monitor more than just system health like CPU usage or latency.

74
00:07:45,070 --> 00:07:49,870
我们必须进行针对 ML 的特定监控，来回答核心问题。
We must perform ML-specific monitoring to answer key questions.

75
00:07:50,570 --> 00:07:53,070
模型的预测准确率仍然很高吗？
Is the model's predictive accuracy still high?

76
00:07:53,610 --> 00:07:59,670
更重要的是，它所看到的现实世界数据是否开始与训练数据产生差异？
And more importantly, has the real-world data it's seeing started to differ from the data it was trained on?

77
00:08:00,110 --> 00:08:04,510
我们监控的最关键的隐性故障之一就是数据漂移。
One of the most critical silent failures we monitor for is data drift.

78
00:08:05,134 --> 00:08:12,310
当生产环境中输入数据的统计特性随时间发生变化，变得与训练数据不同时，就会发生这种情况。
This occurs when the statistical properties of the input data in
production change over time, becoming different from the training data.

79
00:08:12,974 --> 00:08:20,230
例如，在全球疫情之前训练的欺诈检测模型，在疫情后可能会看到非常不同的用户消费模式。
For example, a fraud detection model trained before a global pandemic might see very different user spending patterns after.

80
00:08:21,006 --> 00:08:25,790
数据漂移是一个重大警报，意味着你的模型对世界的认知已经过时了。
Data drift is a major warning sign that your model's view of the world is now outdated.

81
00:08:26,470 --> 00:08:28,970
另一个微妙的问题是概念漂移。
Another subtle issue is concept drift.

82
00:08:29,518 --> 00:08:36,549
在这种情况下，输入数据的统计特征可能保持不变，但输入与输出之间的关系发生了变化。
Here, the input data statistics might stay the same, but the relationship between the inputs and the output changes.

83
00:08:36,549 --> 00:08:45,910
例如，在房价模型中，一个理想特征的概念可能会随时间变化，比如家庭办公室变得更有价值。
For instance, in a housing price model, the concept of a desirable feature might change over time,
like a home office becoming much more valuable.

84
00:08:46,542 --> 00:08:50,170
特征本身没有漂移，但它们的含义变了。
The features themselves haven't drifted, but their meaning has.

85
00:08:50,734 --> 00:08:54,570
这更难检测，但对模型性能的损害同样严重。
This is harder to detect but equally damaging to model performance.

86
00:08:55,246 --> 00:08:58,510
这让我们回到了原点，完成了 MLOps 的闭环。
This brings us full circle, closing the MOps loop.

87
00:08:58,990 --> 00:09:07,110
当我们的监控系统检测到显著的数据漂移、概念漂移或性能下降时，它不仅仅是给人工发封邮件。
When our monitoring system detects significant data drift, concept drift
or performance degradation, it doesn't just send an email to a human.

88
00:09:07,630 --> 00:09:11,370
相反，它作为我们自动化反馈循环的触发器。
Instead, it acts as the trigger for our automated feedback loop.

89
00:09:11,930 --> 00:09:22,330
此警报会自动启动持续训练 CT 流水线，它会拉取
最新的生产数据，重新训练、验证并重新部署模型。
This alert automatically initiates the continuous training CT pipeline, which
pulls in the latest production data, retrains, validates, and redeploys the model.

90
00:09:22,926 --> 00:09:26,610
这就是 MLOps 如何创建真正具有自适应能力的 AI 系统。
This is how Mops creates truly adaptive AI systems.

91
00:09:27,350 --> 00:09:30,790
企业不可能一夜之间就达到这种自动化水平。
Organizations don't achieve this level of automation overnight.

92
00:09:30,830 --> 00:09:35,070
MLOps 的落地是一个经历不同成熟阶段的过程。
ML Ops adoption is a journey through different maturity levels.

93
00:09:35,854 --> 00:09:40,990
它通常从 0 级开始，那是充满了痛点的完全手动流程。
It typically starts at Level 0, a completely manual process full of pain points.

94
00:09:41,690 --> 00:09:46,850
1 级引入了 ML 流水线的自动化，但部署仍然是手动完成的。
Level 1 introduces automation for the ML pipeline but keeps deployment manual.

95
00:09:47,470 --> 00:09:59,030
最终目标是 2 级，它实现了完整的 CI/CD 自动化，能够快速、可靠地更新，
构建出一个可以高效率改进和重新部署的系统。
The ultimate goal is Level 2, which achieves full CICD automation for rapid, reliable updates,
creating a system that can be improved and redeployed with high velocity.

96
00:09:59,030 --> 00:10:07,370
最后，必须记住，MLOps 不仅仅是工具和自动化，它关乎于人和协作。
Finally, it's crucial to remember that MLOps is not just about tools and automation, it's about people and collaboration.

97
00:10:08,150 --> 00:10:16,050
成功的 MLOps 文化能打破数据科学家、ML 工程师和 DevOps 运维团队之间的隔阂。
A successful MLOps culture breaks down the silos between data scientists, ML engineers, and DevOps operations teams.

98
00:10:16,750 --> 00:10:24,670
这些角色在跨职能团队中协同工作，每个人都贡献自己的专业知识来构建和维护 AI 工厂。
These roles work together in cross-functional teams, each bringing their unique expertise to build and maintain the AI factory.

99
00:10:25,358 --> 00:10:30,970
清晰的沟通和共同的责任感与 CI/CD 流水线同样重要。
Clear communication and shared ownership are just as important as the CICD pipeline.

100
00:10:31,790 --> 00:10:42,070
总之，MLOps 将机器学习从一种以研究为导向的手工
活，转变为一种规范化、自动化且可扩展的工程实践。
In summary, MLOps transforms machine learning from a research-oriented manual
craft into a disciplined, automated, and scalable engineering practice.

101
00:10:42,570 --> 00:10:53,170
通过构建这个 AI 工厂，企业可以更快地部署模型，更
可靠地管理模型，降低风险，并不断适应变化的世界。
By building this AI factory, organizations can deploy models faster, manage
them more reliably, mitigate risks, and continuously adapt to a changing world.

102
00:10:53,646 --> 00:11:02,050
它是至关重要的桥梁，将数据科学家笔记本中极具前景的模型，
转化为在现实世界中创造真实且持续的价值。
